<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles Anthony, Prince of Hohenzollern</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1811–1885</span> · Also known as Karl Anton of Hohenzollern</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles Anthony was the last sovereign Prince of Hohenzollern-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigmaringen">Sigmaringen</a>, from 1848, and ceded his principality to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in 1849–1850. He served as Prussian minister-president from 1858 to 1862 during the liberal 'New Era' of the regency of William I. His son Charles became Prince, later King Carol I, of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>, and another son, Leopold, was the candidate for the Spanish throne in 1870.</p></div>
